/**
 * @defgroup Foundation_Time Time
 * @ingroup Foundation
 * @brief Clock abstractions and time utilities.
 *
 * Time models a monotonic wrapping counter and the values derived from it. A
 * Clock binds a raw counter callback and a Frequency; `Now()` combines the
 * current value with the identity of that Clock in a TimePoint. Duration stores
 * a validated elapsed count, while Frequency and Period describe the scale of
 * each tick. `FOUNDATION_TIME` enables this complete family. TypeTraits is a
 * required module dependency because Tick representations are constrained at
 * compile time.
 *
 * @section FoundationTimeHeaders Public Headers
 *
 * | Need | Header |
 * | ---- | ------ |
 * | Entire Foundation library | `#include <Foundation.h>` |
 * | Entire Time module | `#include <Foundation_Time.h>` |
 * | Nested module umbrella | `#include <Foundation/Time.h>` |
 * | One time type | `#include <Foundation/Time/<Type>.h>` |
 *
 * @section FoundationTimeTypes Public Types
 *
 * | Type | Meaning |
 * | ---- | ------- |
 * | @ref Foundation_Time_Tick "Tick" | `Tick<T = uint32_t>` plus the explicit `Tick8`, `Tick16`, `Tick32`, and `Tick64` specializations. |
 * | @ref Foundation_Time_Frequency "Frequency" | Ticks per second as a ratio. |
 * | @ref Foundation_Time_Period "Period" | Seconds per tick as a ratio. |
 * | @ref Foundation_Time_Duration "Duration" | `BasicDuration<TickType>` and its default 32-bit alias `Duration`. |
 * | @ref Foundation_Time_TimePoint "TimePoint" | `BasicTimePoint<TickType>` and its default 32-bit alias `TimePoint`. |
 * | @ref Foundation_Time_Clock "Clock" | `BasicClock<TickType>` and its default 32-bit alias `Clock`. |
 *
 * @section FoundationTimeUsage Basic Usage
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * Foundation::Time::Tick32::Representation ReadTick();
 *
 * Foundation::Time::Clock clock(ReadTick, Foundation::Time::Frequency(1000, 1));
 *
 * const Foundation::Time::TimePoint start = clock.Now();
 * // Work performed here...
 * const Foundation::Time::TimePoint end = clock.Now();
 * const Foundation::Time::Duration elapsed = end - start;
 * if (elapsed.IsValid()) {
 *     const float milliseconds = elapsed.Milliseconds(clock.GetPeriod());
 * }
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section FoundationTimeRepresentations Tick Representations
 *
 * `Tick<T>` is a strongly typed raw counter value. Its representation defaults
 * to `uint32_t` and must satisfy `TypeTraits::is_unsigned_integer<T>`; signed
 * integers, floating-point values, classes, and `bool` are rejected at compile
 * time. The standard aliases are exact specializations:
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * using Tick8  = Tick<uint8_t>;
 * using Tick16 = Tick<uint16_t>;
 * using Tick32 = Tick<uint32_t>;
 * using Tick64 = Tick<uint64_t>;
 * @endcode
 *
 * `Tick<>`, `Tick<uint32_t>`, and `Tick32` are the same type. Foundation does
 * not add a separate non-template `Tick` alias. The short names `Duration`,
 * `TimePoint`, and `Clock` use their `Tick32` template defaults; another width
 * is selected through the corresponding generic type:
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * using TimerClock = Foundation::Time::BasicClock<
 *     Foundation::Time::Tick16
 * >;
 * using TimerDuration = Foundation::Time::BasicDuration<
 *     Foundation::Time::Tick16
 * >;
 * @endcode
 *
 * Scheduling provides matching `Basic...<TickType>` templates, so a selected
 * Tick width can flow from Clock through tasks and TaskScheduler without
 * runtime conversion.
 *
 * @section FoundationTimeModel Modular Time and Validity
 *
 * - Every bit pattern is a valid raw Tick. Tick itself does not decide whether
 *   two counter samples are chronologically comparable.
 * - Duration is valid from zero through one less than the Tick half-range. For
 *   `Tick32`, that is `0..2,147,483,647` ticks. Larger construction values,
 *   arithmetic overflow, and subtraction underflow produce an invalid Duration.
 * - `Duration::IsValid()` distinguishes invalid arithmetic from a real zero
 *   duration. Conversion methods return zero for an invalid Duration.
 * - A default TimePoint has no Clock and `IsValid()` returns false.
 * - Raw counter samples enter the model through `Clock::Now()` or
 *   `Clock::At(ticks)`. TimePoint arithmetic may derive new points while
 *   preserving that identity. The raw identity constructor is not public, so
 *   callers cannot attach a point to an unrelated Clock.
 * - Compatible TimePoints are ordered using modular half-range arithmetic.
 *   This correctly handles one counter rollover when the actual separation is
 *   less than half the selected Tick range.
 * - Subtracting a chronologically earlier compatible point from a later point
 *   returns a valid Duration. Reverse subtraction, the exactly-half-range case,
 *   invalid points, and different Clock identities return an invalid Duration.
 * - Relational operators return false when points have different Clock
 *   identities or their order is ambiguous.
 * - TimePoint stores a non-owning Clock pointer. Clock is neither copyable nor
 *   movable, which keeps its object identity stable; it must still outlive
 *   every point, task, and scheduler that references it.
 * - Frequency and Period are backed by Math::UnsignedRatio. Both numerator and
 *   denominator must be non-zero; zero represents an invalid or unconfigured
 *   value rather than a frequency or period with an undefined reciprocal.
 * - Every valid Frequency has a valid reciprocal Period and vice versa.
 *   Invalid numeric conversions return zero and reciprocal conversions return
 *   an invalid value of the opposite type.
 * - Duration conversion requires the Period belonging to the relevant Clock.
 *
 * @section FoundationTimeExamples Runnable Examples
 *
 * The examples `Foundation_Time_Frequency`, `Foundation_Time_Period`, and
 * `Foundation_Time_ClockAndDuration` demonstrate construction, conversion,
 * mutation, clock identity, arithmetic, and units. See
 * @ref Foundation_Examples "Examples" for build and launch instructions.
 */

/**
 * @namespace Foundation::Time
 * @ingroup Foundation_Time
 * @brief Tick sources, time values, and unit conversions.
 */

/** @defgroup Foundation_Time_Tick Tick
 * @ingroup Foundation_Time
 * @brief Width-explicit unsigned wrapping counter representations. */

/** @defgroup Foundation_Time_Duration Duration
 * @ingroup Foundation_Time
 * @brief Validated elapsed tick counts and unit conversion. */

/** @defgroup Foundation_Time_TimePoint Time Point
 * @ingroup Foundation_Time
 * @brief Modular counter samples associated with a Clock identity. */

/** @defgroup Foundation_Time_Clock Clock
 * @ingroup Foundation_Time
 * @brief Callback-backed tick source with a frequency. */
